course: dictionary
lesson: 8169
title: Residential: where people live
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Residential» describes places where people live in homes, rather than places for shops or factories. Look at the words around it to find the clue. In a «residential street», the word street tells you there are houses on it, not shops.
explain: «On a residential trip (one where you stay away overnight) you label your things.» The brackets give you the meaning straight away: a residential trip is one where you stay away from home overnight.
explain: «Canada has apologised for the residential schools and is working towards reconciliation.» Here residential schools were schools where children lived away from home. Apologised means said sorry, and reconciliation means making things right again between people. This is a sad part of history, so read it with a grown-up if you like.
fact: «Residential» means to do with living in a place.
fact: A residential area is an area where people live in homes, rather than shops or factories.
fact: A residential trip is one where you stay away from home overnight.
fact: Speed limits are often lower in residential streets, because people live there and children may be playing outside.
fact: In Canada, «residential schools» were schools where many Indigenous children were taken from their families, and many were treated badly. Canada has apologised for them.
exercise: «On a residential trip (one where you stay away overnight) you label your things.» What is a residential trip? | A trip to the shops | One where you only go out for the day | A trip by bus only | *One where you stay away from home overnight
exercise: «Canada has apologised for the residential schools and is working towards reconciliation.» Find and copy the word that means saying sorry. | reconciliation | residential | *apologised | Canada
exercise: Which of these is a residential area? | A big factory making cars | A shopping centre full of shops | *A quiet street of houses where families live | An empty field with no buildings
test: What does a residential trip mean? | *Staying away from home for a few nights | Walking to school | Visiting a museum in the morning | Going somewhere for only one hour
test: Why is the speed limit lower in residential streets? | *Because people live there and children may be playing outside | Because there are no cars at all | Because the road is longer | Because the roads are bigger there
exam: In «residential schools», what does residential describe? | Schools built next to the sea | Schools with a very big playground | Schools that are closed on Sundays | *Schools where children lived away from home
